diff --git a/third_party/voice-detect.cpp/third_party/ggml-patches/0001-ggml-cuda-cudnn-conv2d-implicit-gemm.patch b/third_party/voice-detect.cpp/third_party/ggml-patches/0001-ggml-cuda-cudnn-conv2d-implicit-gemm.patch
index bc280df..88835ec 100644
--- a/third_party/voice-detect.cpp/third_party/ggml-patches/0001-ggml-cuda-cudnn-conv2d-implicit-gemm.patch
+++ b/third_party/voice-detect.cpp/third_party/ggml-patches/0001-ggml-cuda-cudnn-conv2d-implicit-gemm.patch
@@ -1,10 +1,43 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: voice-detect.cpp <noreply@localai.io>
+Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: cuDNN implicit-GEMM forward conv for CONV_2D
+
+Opt-in cuDNN path for GGML_OP_CONV_2D, avoiding the im2col global-memory
+spill of the native kernel. Enabled with -DGGML_CUDA_USE_CUDNN=ON; the
+F32-only, NCHW-only, uncached-shape-during-capture cases all fall back to
+ggml_cuda_op_conv2d, so this is never a correctness risk.
+
+Ported to ggml 1.0.0. Two hunks needed re-anchoring, both context drift
+rather than API change:
+
+  - src/ggml-cuda/CMakeLists.txt: the original anchored after
+    GGML_CUDA_PEER_MAX_BATCH_SIZE, which 1.0.0 removed. The block only needs
+    the ggml-cuda target to exist, so it now sits immediately after
+    ggml_add_backend_library(ggml-cuda ...), before the GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS
+    block. Content is otherwise identical.
+  - src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu: the include hunk's context shifted by one
+    line (conv2d-dw.cuh was added upstream); the dispatch hunk moved from
+    line 3041 to 2959. Both applied unchanged once re-anchored.
+
+The 296-line cudnn-conv.cu needed no changes: it uses only
+ggml_backend_cuda_context (ctx.device, ctx.stream()), ggml_is_contiguous,
+ggml_tensor fields, and the cudnn/cuda runtime API, all unchanged in 1.0.0.
+The op_params layout it reads is still s0,s1,p0,p1,d0,d1 at indices 0-5 with
+no c7 slot, and op_params is zero-initialised, so its p[6] cwhn guard is a
+safe no-op.
+
+NOT COMPILED: no CUDA toolchain was available to verify this builds. The
+CMake parses and every symbol it references exists in 1.0.0, but the .cu
+itself has not been through nvcc.
+---
